// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The arguments
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<Useful variations must have occurred>: Two conditions Darwin says cannot be disputed, the advantage that complexity confers on diversity, and the analogy with variations useful to man, together make the absence of any useful variation extraordinary.
    {
    fidelity: "compression"
    note: "Darwin's own 'If ... if ... then, considering ...' supplies the linkage: the premises work only together, and removing any one leaves the rest supporting nothing. The argument is an analogy with the domestic case, and it concludes to what would be extraordinary rather than to a demonstration."
    }

<Useful variations must have occurred>

(1) [Organic beings vary]
(2) [A severe struggle for life]
(3) [Diversity is advantageous]
(4) [Variations useful to man have occurred]
-----
(5) [It would be extraordinary if no useful variation had occurred]

<Preservation of favourable variations>: Given that useful variations occur and that the struggle for life is severe, the individuals that have them are preserved, and by the strong principle of inheritance leave offspring like themselves.
    {
    fidelity: "compression"
    note: "The structure is Darwin's - 'assuredly ... and from the strong principle of inheritance ...' - but its first premise is the reconstruction's detachment of his conditional, and carries the interpretation marker for it."
    }

<Preservation of favourable variations>

(1) [Useful variations occur]
(2) [A severe struggle for life]
-----
(3) [The favoured are preserved]
(4) [The principle of inheritance is strong]
-----
(5) [The favoured leave offspring like themselves]

<Diversification pays>: During the modification of the descendants of a species, and the incessant struggle of all species to increase in numbers, the more diversified those descendants become the better their chance of succeeding.
    {
    fidelity: "interpretation"
    warrant: "coherence"
    note: "Darwin's 'Therefore' opens the second paragraph on the far side of an ellipsis, so his ground for this step is in the omitted material. The premises drawn here are the two circumstances his own sentence names, which is what the excerpt offers and is less than the 'Therefore' claims."
    }

<Diversification pays>

(1) [The favoured leave offspring like themselves]
(2) [A severe struggle for life]
-----
(3) [Diversification improves the chance of success]

<Varieties grow into species>: If diversification pays and useful differences are inherited, the small differences between varieties will grow until they equal the differences between species, or even between genera.
    {
    fidelity: "compression"
    note: "Darwin's 'Thus' gathers the whole preceding argument. The second premise is his own conclusion about inheritance, without which differences could be advantageous without accumulating."
    }

<Varieties grow into species>

(1) [Diversification improves the chance of success]
(2) [The favoured leave offspring like themselves]
-----
(3) [Varietal differences grow into specific differences]

<The excerpt omits the ground of divergence>: The excerpt elides the material between its two paragraphs, so what licenses the step to diversification is not in the text that is given. #contested
    {
    fidelity: "interpretation"
    warrant: "the excerpt's own elisions"
    note: "This objection is the reconstruction's own - not Darwin's, and not a critic's. It grants both premises of the diversification step and denies that the excerpt shows them licensing its conclusion, so it is an undercut and not an attack. Read against the whole of the Origin it would be a bad objection; read against this passage it is the honest one, because the argument it asks for is exactly what the ellipsis removed."
    }

<The excerpt omits the ground of divergence>

(1) [The excerpt marks an omission before the second paragraph]
(2) [The omitted material is not restored]
-----
(3) [The excerpt does not display the ground of diversification]

